WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.130
Usually one machine holds

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:03.370
one subscription.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.250
Claude Max on the MacBook,

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.110
ChatGPT Pro on the Linux

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:07.790
box.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.340
SpecWithCode connects

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:10.820
them over Tailscale and

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.360
watches every limit and

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:13.060
reset.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.210
You talk to one coordinator.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:16.630
It starts threads,

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.110
each with its own pull

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:18.730
request.

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:20.420
Auto-resolve closes a

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:21.640
thread only when it's

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:22.320
merged,

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.820
green and approved.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.430
Linux for speed,

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.030
the Mac to orchestrate.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:28.550
SpecWithCode,

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:31.530
open source at specwithcode.dev.
